  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening quality assurance in higher education in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In December 2014 the African Member States adopted the Addis Convention. The Implementation of the Convention requires human and institutional capacity building in quality assurance and development of mechanisms and tools that would ensure comparability and compatibility of qualifications through transparent, fair and efficient assessment processes. The project foresees strengthening of quality assurance of higher education structure in 10 African countries. Its activities will focus on establishing 5(five) new Quality Assurance Agencies, reinforce structures in 5 others, and consolidate the existing QA networks in Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
